          "intro": "Citește materialul profesoarei de mai jos, apoi urmărește explicațiile practice asociate. Această lecție păstrează contextul complet al sursei, inclusiv variantele vechi și comentariile.",
          "example": "# INFO ID 2026 — Complete learning issue roadmap\n\nThis consolidated draft replaces the earlier 51-issue draft. It contains 86 numbered tasks: 80 website tasks and 6 isolated study exercises. Issue 002 is the explicitly requested clickable-logo addition; the remaining mechanisms follow the supplied teacher archive. Page placement, section organization and implemented features must match the teacher; only the agreed class-related content changes. Numbers below are roadmap IDs, not GitHub issue numbers. Do not create any issues automatically.\n\nVerified on 2026-10-13 against the supplied exemplu_cofetarie_19_oct archive and [Website main at 55e6abce3a955b05210a033ae5511870c16675a0](https://github.com/infoid26/Website/tree/55e6abce3a955b05210a033ae5511870c16675a0).\n\n## Agreed content mapping\n\n| Teacher content | Class website equivalent |\n|---|---|\n| Product / cake | A subject |\n| Product name and description | Subject name and description |\n| Ingredients | Concepts to learn |\n| Price | Estimated study time in minutes |\n| Calories | Number of pages to study |\n| Weight | Number of chapters |\n| Product category | Subject domain, such as mathematics/programming/web, using the team's actual list |\n| Product type | Semester, using the team's actual list |\n| Product boolean | Whether introductory material is available; complete with team-confirmed information |\n| Product image and timestamp | Subject image and addition date |\n| Virtual basket | Saved selection of subject IDs |\n| Promotions / recipe content | Team-supplied study activities / selected study videos |\n\nThe user confirmed the subject/concept/numeric/domain/semester mapping. The boolean is a proposed equivalent of the existing database field; it adds no new flow. Real subjects, concepts, semesters, chapter/page counts, estimated minutes, notices, contact information, images and videos must be provided or verified by the team. Mark practice data clearly. No unverified curriculum or official announcements are supplied here.\n\nTeacher references below are paths relative to the root of your own local copy of exemplu_cofetarie_19_oct. A suffix such as :277 means line 277. Open those files locally to compare the examples.\n\n## How to use the roadmap\n\n1. Open the source path listed in each issue before changing our site. Dependencies refer to roadmap IDs.\n2. Use HTML first, then CSS, small browser scripts, Node/EJS, SCSS, JSON/images, PostgreSQL and catalog scripts. Open only issues whose prerequisites are available; do not assign later database tasks to someone who has not practiced the earlier stages.\n3. Preserve existing variable/function names. Moving content into the homepage, resurse or EJS is not a reason to rename reused code. New names should be agreed in the implementing issue.\n4. Match the teacher's structure: FAQ questions belong on the homepage inside index-intrebari. Move reusable existing FAQ content there, remove the dedicated page and its search/category/sidebar features, and learn the teacher's details/summary, counters and open-state styles in that section.\n5. Reuse existing completed work. Reuse base metadata, community links, .gitignore and node_modules exclusion. Reuse menu and FAQ content while reshaping their structure to match the teacher. Items below extend specific missing mechanisms. A CSS feature and its later SCSS conversion are separate learning steps of the same component, not two components.\n6. A website task is done when its behavior works and the author can explain it. A study exercise is done in a practice copy and produces a short explanation, without adding a feature to the class site. Include the manual checks and the files touched in the PR.\n7. Every student should perform the source exercise on a personal copy of the teacher's project. Assigning one issue to one student does not teach the other students that feature. During review, ask the author to explain a line and make a small related change.\n8. The drills are practice suggestions based on the supplied source. They are not confirmed exam questions and do not establish the full examination syllabus.\n\n## Existing GitHub work to reuse\n\n| Existing work | Verified state / action |\n|---|---|\n| [#1 Base HTML](https://github.com/infoid26/Website/issues/1) | Open; base skeleton exists on main. Use the relevant new section tasks as scoped follow-up work rather than recreating the skeleton. |\n| [#2 README](https://github.com/infoid26/Website/issues/2) | Open; use it for local-run and contributor documentation as the server evolves. |\n| [#5 .gitignore](https://github.com/infoid26/Website/issues/5), [#6 node_modules](https://github.com/infoid26/Website/issues/6) | Open, but the file and node_modules exclusion already exist on main. Verify acceptance and resolve those existing issues instead of creating duplicates. |",
