          "example": "<a id=\"issue-008\"></a>\n\n### 008. Move the existing FAQ into the homepage, matching the teacher's structure\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** HTML.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `index.html`; `views/pagini/index.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [003](#issue-003).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Read the teacher's index-intrebari section: details/summary questions are part of the homepage, not a separate page.\n2. Move reusable question/answer content from our current faq.html into one homepage section with id index-intrebari and an h2. Retain native details/summary behavior and the agreed class content. Remove the dedicated FAQ destination, search panel, category controls, sidebar and faq.js inclusion from the target site; those features are not implemented in the teacher's FAQ. Preserve reusable names and do not rename functions as part of this task.\n3. Update FAQ navigation to the homepage section anchor. Remove the obsolete standalone FAQ file from the target site once its content has been transferred; Git history preserves the previous implementation.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] FAQ questions appear exactly once, on the homepage, and open/close using native details/summary. The FAQ navigation targets #index-intrebari from the homepage and the corresponding homepage anchor from other pages once they exist.\n- [ ] No dedicated FAQ page, FAQ search script, category filter, sidebar or duplicated answers remain in the target structure. Subsequent EJS conversion keeps the FAQ in views/pagini/index.ejs.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Add one details/summary pair inside index-intrebari and change its answer; explain why no separate page or JavaScript handler is required.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-009\"></a>\n\n### 009. Add presentation figures and a static gallery\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** HTML.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `index.html`; `views/pagini/index.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [003](#issue-003).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Use figure, img and figcaption for presentation images and one static gallery. The teacher has three explicitly placed figures plus a fourth unassigned figure in the current version; study that distinction. Use supplied class-related images.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Each meaningful image has suitable alt text and a caption. The presentation and gallery reuse images only when intentional; no second gallery page is created.",
