          "referenceText": "- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Change rotateX and explain the stacking and positioning of each wrapper.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-037\"></a>\n\n### 037. Style video captions with cue selectors\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** CSS.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/css/video.css`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [012](#issue-012), [036](#issue-036).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Use ::cue to style caption background, color and font size, including the teacher's 1000px media variation.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] When captions are enabled, both language tracks use the intended cue style.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Change only caption text color and explain why an ordinary p selector cannot style the cues.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-038\"></a>\n\n### 038. Switch light and dark themes through a button event\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Browser JavaScript.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/js/schimba_tema.js`; `resurse/css/general.css`; `views/fragmente/header.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [017](#issue-017).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Add one theme button and a DOMContentLoaded handler. Use getElementById and classList.toggle on body.dark, starting with event handling and conditions before persistence.",
