          "example": "\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Study and implement setCookie, getCookie and deleteCookie, using Date, UTC expiry, template literals, split, trim, startsWith and return. Keep the teacher's function names when using them.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] A cookie can be created, read and expired on the same HTTP origin. Explain cookies versus localStorage and test the effective cookie path.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Create a short-lived practice cookie, retrieve it, expire it and explain each result.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-041\"></a>\n\n### 041. Add the school-project banner and remember acceptance\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Browser JavaScript.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/js/cookies.js`; `views/fragmente/footer.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [040](#issue-040), [014](#issue-014).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Add the teacher's project banner and acceptance button to the footer. Read acceptat_banner on load and hide the banner when accepted; preserve the example's 60000ms expiry.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The banner hides after acceptance, stays hidden on reload while the cookie remains valid, and reappears after expiry. Verify behavior across homepage and secondary-page paths.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Change the expiry to a short interval and explain the resulting behavior.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-042\"></a>\n\n### 042. Create the Node package and understand dependency installation\n",
