          "example": "**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Node and EJS.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `package.json`; `package-lock.json`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [001](#issue-001).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Create our package.json for the server stage and initially install Express and EJS. Inspect the teacher's remaining dependencies, installing them in their own later tasks. Keep node_modules excluded by the existing .gitignore.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] package.json and the lockfile are versioned; node_modules is not. The author can explain require, dependency versions and why the teacher's test script is a placeholder.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Explain what npm install restores from a clean checkout and why node_modules is not a source file.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-043\"></a>\n\n### 043. Run an Express server and serve existing static resources\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Node and EJS.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `index.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [042](#issue-042).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Create the server entry point using require, express, path, express.static and listen. Serve the current homepage for this intermediate step and resources at /resurse. Use localhost:8080 as in the example. Add the teacher's explicit /favicon.ico route using res.sendFile.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The homepage can be opened over HTTP and their assets load through the server. Explain that shared development uses Git branches/PRs rather than simultaneous edits to one checkout.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Change the port and one resource route; explain which URLs change.\n\n---",
