          "duration": "3–6 min",
          "referenceText": "\n<a id=\"issue-053\"></a>\n\n### 053. Express the existing menu styles with SCSS nesting\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** SCSS and Bootstrap.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/scss/nav1.scss`; `resurse/css/nav1.css`; `resurse/css/nav.css`; `resurse/lectiile_urmatoare/scss/nav.scss`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [028](#issue-028), [052](#issue-052).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Translate our existing menu rules into nested SCSS with & hover selectors, preserving selectors. Inspect the teacher's nav1.scss versus linked nav.css mismatch and deliberately choose the output the page loads.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Compiled CSS preserves the menu behavior; the page references the generated file that actually changes. Do not maintain two competing editable menu implementations.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Expand one nested selector by hand and check the compiled result.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-054\"></a>\n\n### 054. Study SCSS placeholders and extend in the small example\n\n**Type:** Study exercise. **Stage:** SCSS and Bootstrap.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/scss/exemplu.scss`; `resurse/css/exemplu.css`; `resurse/scss/output.css`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [050](#issue-050).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Use the teacher's %grup-util and @extend example in an isolated practice copy. Explain reusable declarations and the generated #box rules; no arbitrary extra box is added to the class homepage.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The exercise compiles and the author can match source declarations to generated selectors. Generated duplicates and map references are recorded as outputs, not separate features.",
