          "example": "\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Connect the error renderer to the named wildcard: reject direct .ejs URLs with 400, resource-folder URLs with 403 and missing views with 404. Study callback errors separately from synchronous try/catch.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The teacher's defined requests display the intended error pages and statuses. Explain that the resource check is specific to these routes, not a general access-control system.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Trigger all three cases and distinguish a render callback error from a thrown exception.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-059\"></a>\n\n### 059. Load gallery metadata into server memory\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Gallery JSON and images.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/json/galerie.json`; `index.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [044](#issue-044), [009](#issue-009).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Install Sharp for the next task and implement the JSON-loading part of initImagini. Use cale_galerie and an array of filename/description/month-list objects.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Metadata comes from one JSON file instead of repeated template values. Entries without luni remain distinguishable from entries with an array.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Remove a month list in a practice JSON file and explain optional data.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-060\"></a>\n\n### 060. Generate gallery thumbnails with Sharp\n",
