          "example": "**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Gallery JSON and images.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `index.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [059](#issue-059).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Create the mediu directory when needed, split source filenames, resize to width 300 and write WebP thumbnails. Add browser-facing original and thumbnail paths to metadata.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] A thumbnail exists at the expected dimensions and format. Handle completion before relying on it; repeated server starts must not treat stale outputs as completed work.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Change the resize width and explain server file paths versus browser URLs.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-061\"></a>\n\n### 061. Render gallery pictures from JSON and filter them by month\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Gallery JSON and images.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `views/pagini/index.ejs`; `index.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [060](#issue-060), [033](#issue-033).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Pass imagini through the homepage route; replace only the static gallery's repeated figures with an EJS loop and picture sources. Use Date.getMonth, includes and optional chaining for month availability.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The current-month entries render with a 1000px thumbnail source. Correct the teacher's ten-month lookup to support all twelve months; entries without luni follow the documented example behavior.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Test October, November and December in a practice copy; add one month to an image.\n\n---",
