          "example": "**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** PostgreSQL and catalog.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `index.js`; `views/fragmente/header.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [068](#issue-068).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Adapt req.query.tip into a semester query parameter and add corresponding catalog submenu destinations. Keep full-catalog and semester-specific routes using the same page. Learn a parameterized WHERE query for the supplied value.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The full catalog and semester-filtered catalog return the expected rows; the browser's later filters operate on those returned rows. Do not concatenate request text into SQL.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Compare a URL query parameter with a browser-only dropdown filter.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-070\"></a>\n\n### 070. Render a subject detail route using a path parameter\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** PostgreSQL and catalog.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `index.js`; `views/pagini/produs.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [068](#issue-068), [057](#issue-057).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Adapt /produs/:id into the subject detail route. Read req.params, query one row using a parameter value, inspect rowCount and render all detail fields, including concept array, boolean and timestamp. Validate the requested ID before querying and reuse the database error case for failed queries.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Both name and image links open the correct subject. An absent ID returns the existing 404 error page; query errors use the existing database error definition.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Change the requested ID and explain req.params versus req.query.\n\n---",
