          "duration": "3–6 min",
          "referenceText": "\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Use getElementsByName, checked, split, destructuring or equivalent array access, parseInt and a loop with break to read the selected interval. Apply lower-inclusive, upper-exclusive page ranges and the All option.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Boundary values are handled explicitly and match the teacher's interval mechanism. Each condition's result can be explained before combining filters.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Test values exactly at both boundaries and change one range.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-077\"></a>\n\n### 077. Combine the minimum-minute and domain filters with the other conditions\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Catalog JavaScript.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/js/produse.js`; `resurse/lectiile_urmatoare/js/produse.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [076](#issue-076).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Parse study minutes with parseFloat, compare against the range minimum, read the selected domain, and combine name/page/minute/domain predicates using logical AND. Study the active >= comparison versus the alternate strict > comparison.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Only subjects matching every chosen condition appear. The chosen boundary behavior is documented and follows the active teacher version; decimals are retained.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Use a value equal to the threshold and explain why >= differs from >.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-078\"></a>\n\n### 078. Reset all filter controls and restore catalog visibility\n",
