          "example": "**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Catalog JavaScript.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/js/produse.js`; `resurse/lectiile_urmatoare/js/produse.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [077](#issue-077).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Implement the reset button. Compare the active script's partial reset with the alternate script's complete reset of text, range, range label, domain and radios; restore all current catalog cards.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Reset restores the complete documented initial state without discarding saved subject selections. The difference between both teacher versions is explained.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Leave a domain selected in a practice reset and demonstrate the inconsistent next filter.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-079\"></a>\n\n### 079. Sort cards by study minutes and then by subject name\n\n**Type:** Website task. **Stage:** Catalog JavaScript.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `resurse/js/produse.js`; `resurse/lectiile_urmatoare/js/produse.js`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [077](#issue-077).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Convert the card collection using Array.from, sort with a comparator, use the primary numeric difference and localeCompare for ties, multiply by direction, and reorder existing nodes with appendChild.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Ascending and descending order are correct including equal-minute names and decimal values. Hidden cards retain their filtering state; no duplicated nodes are created.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Reverse the direction and explain why the alternate version's parseInt can lose decimal precision.\n\n---",
