          "title": "issues-roadmap-en.md · 2296–2340",
          "intro": "Citește materialul profesoarei de mai jos, apoi urmărește explicațiile practice asociate. Această lecție păstrează contextul complet al sursei, inclusiv variantele vechi și comentariile.",
          "example": "\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. Analyze the ingredient group's arrays and ingredient-name dictionary with quantity/unit/calories. In a practice copy map these structures to concept groups and per-concept properties without creating a new study calculator. Note that anunturi.json is empty.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The learner distinguishes arrays, nested objects, keyed lookup and numeric properties. No behavior is claimed for files that no route or script reads.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Retrieve one dictionary entry through a group member's name and modify one nested value.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"issue-086\"></a>\n\n### 086. Study the supplied user and access-log database schema\n\n**Type:** Study exercise. **Stage:** Study-only source files.\n\n**Teacher reference:** `utilizatori.sql`; `index.js`; `views/fragmente/header.ejs`.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [064](#issue-064).\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Open and read the referenced example and identify the elements, selectors, functions or data used by this task.\n2. In a disposable study database inspect the roles enum, users table, serial IDs, required values, unique username, defaults and access-log foreign key with nullable user_id. Do not add login, registration, email confirmation or tracking routes: the archive has no such implementations.\n3. Check the acceptance criteria below and record the result in the PR or study notes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] The learner explains the schema and relationship; menu placeholders, uploaded-image folders and MongoDB null fields are not presented as implemented features.\n- [ ] Explain the changed source and complete the practice modification below without simply copying a finished solution.\n\n**Practice modification in the teacher's project:** Attempt an access row with a nonexistent user ID and explain the foreign-key failure.\n\n---\n\n## Technical references for necessary corrections\n\nParameter values from URLs should be passed separately to SQL, using [node-postgres parameterized queries](https://node-postgres.com/features/queries); this keeps the same teacher feature while correcting direct string interpolation. Template syntax is documented by [EJS](https://ejs.co/). The teacher uses Express 5.1.0; named wildcard matching and root handling are documented in the [Express 5 migration guide](https://expressjs.com/en/guide/migrating-5/). These references support implementation correctness, not additional product features.\n",
